cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Meta Science Arena or cite a score from it, please cite this software."
title: "Meta Science Arena"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible benchmark arenas for meta-science tools. Each arena is a focused
  task family with known ground truth — extracting statistics from a paper,
  detecting a preregistration deviation, checking GRIM consistency — on which
  tools, platforms and language models are scored against the same tasks. Task
  generation is seed-deterministic, scoring is contamination-controlled, and
  every published score traces back to a raw run record.
type: software
authors:
